# implements-port slice 13: a compound size_t value (`b + 1U`) into an unsigned own at the root --
# convert.lm2 has no such row.  Only the walk types a compound value, so this reaches the root's
# own refusal (l2_rw_convert), with the phrase a method uses (unit_s7_conv_norow); a single value is
# refused earlier by the root's assignment check, with the same phrase.  Mutant: none -- this row
# pins that the branch refuses.
unsigned: u 0U
size_t: b 2U
u: b + 1U
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
